    "statement": "The O x W crossover is SIGN-STABLE across seed cohort and settle depth: the long-range-ROUTING fault (W) is sociality-selective and the CAPACITY fault (O) is capacity-selective, on every cell. The autism(W) / ID(O) double dissociation stands as an in-silico [L]: two SEPARABLE axes, not one factor. HONEST RESIDUALS: the dissociation is a RELATIVE selectivity (a crossover) -- each fault has a small off-target effect (W nicks capacity ~0.06; O perturbs sociality <=0.03) but hits its target ~2-3x harder; and the effect is gene-blind (g absent from sign() dynamics) and a micro-model property (organ-scale single-tract lesion is not sign-stable). The clinical labels stay an INTERPRETATION held at arm's length -- this is an in-silico phase/autoassociator result, NOT a clinical measure."
